    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46268" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζιγγίβερις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>Edict.Diocl.</u>
			32.68
		</span></i> (<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Delph., Clit.</i>),
				ὁ<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ἡ</span>
			(both in <u>Edict.Diocl.</u> l.c.); or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζιγγίβερι</span></b> , τό, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
			</span></i> (codd. opt.) and <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc.:—an Arabian spice-plant, the root of which was
			used in medicine, prob. <i>ginger</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.160
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.572
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.880
			</span></i>. (Perh. fr. Malay <i>inchi-ver</i> (<i>inchi</i>
			= root) through Skt.
				<i>śṛ[ndot  ]gaveram</i> and a Prakrit
				<i>singaber.</i>)</div>
